Lab 19: Disaster Recovery and Backup Planning for Red Hat Satellite 6
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the importance of disaster recovery planning for Red Hat Satellite infrastructure
Create comprehensive backups of the Satellite database and configuration files using scripted procedures
Implement automated backup scheduling using cron
Restore Satellite database and configuration data from backup in a controlled test environment
Validate backup integrity and document disaster recovery procedures for operational use
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Red Hat Satellite 6 architecture and components (Foreman, Candlepin, Pulp)
Knowledge of PostgreSQL database concepts
Understanding of file system operations, permissions, and shell scripting
Access to a Satellite 6 server (or a Linux VM used to simulate one) with root or sudo access
This lab assumes access to a Red Hat Satellite 6 server. If a live Satellite installation is not available, the backup and restore scripts can still be exercised against the local PostgreSQL instance and a set of representative configuration directories, since the scripting and recovery concepts transfer directly to a real Satellite deployment. No additional packages beyond those already present on a standard Satellite server are required. If PostgreSQL client tools are missing on a plain test VM, install them with:

sudo dnf install -y postgresql postgresql-server rsync tar gzip
